1.2 Covered Project. "Covered Project" means DaveLM, the development codename "Baby," and any successor name, rebrand, release line, model family, or project component that is expressly distributed with this License or identified as governed by LicenseRef-DaveLM-Research-1.0.

1.3 Covered Materials. "Covered Materials" means, to the extent owned or licensable by Licensor: source code, scripts, configuration, architecture files, tokenizer files and configuration, model weights, checkpoints, adapters, sidecars, training and evaluation code, documentation, model cards, manifests, evaluation artifacts, test suites, prompts created as project assets, data files created by Licensor, packaging, release artifacts, and authorized derivatives of the foregoing that are distributed under this License.

1.4 Excluded Materials. Covered Materials do not include third-party materials, public-domain material, facts, ideas, methods, algorithms, interfaces, or other subject matter that Licensor does not own or is not legally entitled to license. Third-party components remain subject to their own terms, notices, and licenses.

1.5 Reservation of Rights. All rights not expressly granted are reserved. No implied license arises from access, disclosure, contribution, compatibility, estoppel, exhaustion beyond applicable law, or any course of dealing. This License is not an open-source license and does not grant a general right to redistribute Covered Materials.

1.6 No Transfer of Ownership. The Covered Materials are licensed, not sold. Possession of a copy does not transfer title, copyright, patent, trademark, trade secret, or other ownership rights.

2. Definitions

2.1 Authorized User. An "Authorized User" is a person or entity that lawfully receives access to Covered Materials from Licensor or an authorized channel and accepts this License. A person who obtains Covered Materials through an unauthorized leak, scrape, mirror, or redistribution is not an Authorized User and receives no permission under this License.

2.2 Non-Commercial Purpose. "Non-Commercial Purpose" means internal personal, educational, academic, or research activity that is not intended for, incorporated into, or used to support revenue generation, paid services, commercial products, advertising, fundraising, customer delivery, employer/client deliverables, competitive commercial advantage, or other direct or indirect commercial benefit.

2.3 Derivative. "Derivative" means a modification or adaptation of Covered Materials, including modified source, fine-tuned or continued-training weights, merged weights, adapters, LoRA or similar parameter deltas, converted/quantized weights, distilled versions, architecture variants derived from protected implementation expression, or a package containing a substantial portion of Covered Materials. The term is contractual and does not attempt to redefine statutory copyright law.

2.4 Model Extraction. "Model Extraction" includes distillation, cloning, imitation training, teacher-student transfer, behavior cloning, systematic output harvesting, reconstruction, inversion, or other activity intended to reproduce or approximate DaveLM capabilities, weights, representations, or behavior in a separate model or system.

2.5 Commercial Use. "Commercial Use" includes sale, resale, licensing, paid consulting, paid research, hosted access, cloud deployment for third parties, software-as-a-service, API access, ad-supported deployment, product integration, enterprise deployment, work-for-hire, customer-facing use, or use that materially supports a commercial organization unless Licensor provides separate written authorization.

