3.1 Grant. Subject to continuous compliance with this License, Licensor grants each Authorized User a limited, worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license to possess, execute, inspect, and internally reproduce Covered Materials solely for a Non-Commercial Purpose.

3.2 Internal Research Modifications. Authorized Users may internally modify source code and may internally fine-tune or otherwise create DaveLM Derivatives solely for a Non-Commercial Purpose. Any such Derivative remains subject to this License while in the Authorized User's possession and may not be distributed, published, sublicensed, transferred, sold, or made available to any third party without separate written permission from Licensor.

3.3 Necessary Internal Copies. Authorized Users may make the minimum number of internal backup and working copies reasonably necessary for permitted use, provided all copyright, license, provenance, and attribution notices are preserved.

3.4 No Other Grant. No permission is granted to distribute, publicly perform, publicly display source in a manner that enables copying, sublicense, commercialize, host for third parties, or create a competing service or model based on Covered Materials except by separate written agreement.

4. Prohibited Uses and Acts

4.1 Commercialization. You must not use Covered Materials or DaveLM Derivatives for Commercial Use without a separate written commercial license signed or otherwise expressly issued by Licensor.

4.2 Redistribution. You must not upload, publish, mirror, seed, transmit, sell, sublicense, gift, share, or otherwise distribute Covered Materials or DaveLM Derivatives to any third party, including through package registries, model hubs, torrents, repositories, cloud storage, container images, or embedded applications, except with Licensor's prior written permission.

4.3 Hosted Access. You must not provide interactive or programmatic third-party access to Covered Materials or DaveLM Derivatives through an API, website, application, bot, remote desktop, managed service, inference endpoint, hosted notebook, or similar service, whether paid or free, unless separately authorized in writing.

4.4 Extraction, Distillation, and Competing Models. You must not conduct Model Extraction or use Covered Materials, DaveLM Derivatives, or DaveLM-generated outputs as a dataset, teacher signal, preference signal, label source, reward signal, benchmark-training target, or synthetic-data source to train, fine-tune, align, distill, calibrate, or otherwise improve a model or model-based system other than an internal DaveLM Derivative permitted by Section 3.2.

4.5 Protected Signals. Without separate written permission, you must not systematically collect or use logits, probabilities, hidden states, activations, attention maps, embeddings, gradients, intermediate tensors, model traces, or large-scale outputs for cloning, reconstruction, training, or competitive analysis.

4.6 Circumvention. You must not bypass, disable, defeat, remove, or interfere with access controls, license checks, attribution mechanisms, provenance metadata, rate limits, safety controls, or technical restrictions that accompany Covered Materials, except solely as necessary for a permitted internal security or compatibility test and only if no restricted material is exposed to a third party.

4.7 Misrepresentation. You must not represent yourself as Licensor, claim official affiliation or endorsement, falsely claim authorship, obscure the origin of Covered Materials, or present a Derivative as an official DaveLM release.

4.8 Removal of Notices. You must not remove, hide, alter, or falsify copyright notices, license notices, provenance information, cryptographic manifests, authorship records, model cards, or third-party notices.

4.9 Unlawful and Rights-Violating Use. You must not use Covered Materials to violate applicable law or the rights of another person, including intellectual-property, privacy, publicity, confidentiality, contractual, or data-protection rights.

4.10 Restricted High-Risk Deployment. Without separate written authorization, you must not deploy Covered Materials as the sole or primary decision-maker in a context where an erroneous output could directly determine a person's eligibility, liberty, medical treatment, employment, credit, insurance, housing, legal rights, or physical safety. This clause does not prohibit non-deployment research or evaluation concerning such domains.

5. Outputs

5.1 No Blanket Ownership Claim. Licensor does not claim ownership of every output merely because it was generated by DaveLM. Ownership and protectability of outputs depend on applicable law and the content involved.

5.2 Reproduced Protected Material. To the extent an output reproduces protectable portions of Covered Materials, this License does not grant rights beyond those expressly stated here.

5.3 Output-Based Training Restriction. Regardless of output ownership, an Authorized User contractually agrees not to use systematic DaveLM outputs, conversations, labels, scores, or synthetic examples to train, fine-tune, distill, align, or improve a non-DaveLM model or service without Licensor's prior written permission.

5.4 Incidental Personal Use of Outputs. This License does not restrict ordinary personal use of isolated outputs created during permitted Non-Commercial use, provided that such use does not disclose Covered Materials, violate Section 4, or imply endorsement by Licensor.

6. Benchmarks, Research Results, and Publications

6.1 Internal Evaluation. Internal benchmarking, red-team testing, error analysis, reproducibility testing, and academic study are permitted for a Non-Commercial Purpose.

6.2 Public Results. You may publish factual high-level benchmark or research results without exposing Covered Materials, provided you: (a) identify the exact DaveLM release tested; (b) disclose material modifications and evaluation methodology; (c) do not publish weights, protected source, non-public evaluation items, or other Covered Materials; (d) do not misrepresent unofficial results as endorsed by Licensor; and (e) preserve required attribution.

6.3 No Benchmark Laundering. You must not use published benchmark results or generated datasets as a workaround to perform Model Extraction, competitive cloning, or prohibited commercial development.

