12. Term and Termination

12.1 Term. This License begins when you first accept or exercise rights under it and continues until terminated.

12.2 Automatic Termination for Material Breach. Your rights automatically terminate upon a material breach. Unauthorized commercialization, redistribution of weights or source, intentional removal of ownership notices, or Model Extraction constitutes a material breach and may result in immediate termination without a cure period.

12.3 Cure for Other Breaches. For a non-willful breach that is reasonably curable and is not listed in Section 12.2, rights may be reinstated if the breach is fully cured within ten (10) calendar days after you become aware of it or receive written notice, whichever occurs first, unless Licensor states in writing that reinstatement is denied because the same or a substantially similar breach has recurred.

12.4 Effect of Termination. Upon termination, you must stop using Covered Materials and, to the extent legally permitted, delete or destroy copies and Derivatives in your possession or control, except archival copies that must be retained by law. Retained archival copies may not be used.

12.5 Survival. Sections concerning ownership, restrictions, outputs used for model training, attribution, confidentiality, termination effects, disclaimers, liability, indemnity, enforcement, and general legal terms survive termination to the extent necessary to give them effect.

